  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n\n// Now\n\nWhat I am doing this month. \n\nA dated list instead of a feed. It changes about once a month, and the status line at the top of the site always matches it.\n\nmain\nsoren/now\ndocs(now): update for October\nedited this week\n\nOpen to work from November\nLast updated 2026-10-06\n\n2026-10-06\nShipping transactions v3 at Kestrel Pay\nThe last table in the dashboard moves to the new engine this month. Target: every interaction under 50 ms on a mid-range laptop.\n2026-10-01\nBooking one project from November\nA build or a performance audit, six to twelve weeks. One project at a time, so the first good fit takes the slot.\n2026-09-22\ntinyvirtual 3.0 is in beta\nVariable row heights without a measuring pass. Breaking changes are written up in the repository before the release.\n2026-09-14\nReading the CSS anchor positioning spec\nSlowly, with a notebook. I want to delete a popover library from two client projects by the end of the year.\n2026-09-02\nNot taking: rewrites without a number\nIf nobody can say how slow the current thing is, the first week is an audit, not a rewrite. I say this before the contract.\n2026-08-18\nOff the grid for one week in August\nHiking in Jotunheimen with no laptop. Messages were answered on the 26th, as promised.\n\nEdited by hand, about once a month. If the date above is older than six weeks, write and ask.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n--:--\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.",
  "url": "https://wild-hours-611915.framer.app/now"
